SPIRV-Tools: the validator's messages leave out the shader's debug source

What: ValidationState_t::diag no longer calls InspectShaderDebugInfo, so an
error message carries the disassembled instruction but not the source lines
that NonSemantic.Shader.DebugInfo names.
Why: Venus runs spirv-val on every guest module (virgl-venus-spirv-validate.
patch). On SPIRV-Tools' own test module ext_inst_debug-503 the printer
(PrintShaderDebugInfoSource) read an operand the module's DebugSource does not
have; operands_.at() past the end under -fno-exceptions calls abort(), which
would end QEMU. The source lines only make messages longer.
Upstream: not reported yet (draft in the lane's upstream-drafts.md).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-spirv-validate.sh (the corpus under
AddressSanitizer, ext_inst_debug-503 among the refused modules).

diff --git a/source/val/validation_state.cpp b/source/val/validation_state.cpp
--- a/source/val/validation_state.cpp
+++ b/source/val/validation_state.cpp
@@ -355,10 +355,12 @@
   }
 
   std::string disassembly;
+  // OmacVM: no shader debug info source in messages: its printer reads the
+  // module's debug instructions unchecked and ended the process on hostile
+  // ones (operands_.at() past the end under -fno-exceptions)
   std::string shader_debug_info;
   if (inst) {
     disassembly = Disassemble(*inst);
-    shader_debug_info = InspectShaderDebugInfo(*inst);
   }
 
   return DiagnosticStream({0, 0, inst ? inst->LineNum() : 0},
